## Flight report

- **Left gate:** crossed around decision k=5→k=6 (crossbar visible passing under the downward camera, forward view opened into the room beyond with no posts left in frame). Alignment before the crossing was uncertain — I never got a clean "both posts on the tick" frame; I tracked a single, mostly-centered post inward and the crossing happened along that heading. Likely through the gate but not confirmed centered through the middle.
- **Center gate:** never found. After clearing the left gate I turned and advanced through open room and then into a cluttered storage/equipment alcove (shelving, crates, cords, a mannequin) that dead-ended at a wall. No yellow posts or teal crossbar were ever seen again in the remaining 7 decisions.
- **Penguin:** never located. No black-and-white shape appeared in the downward camera at any point after the left gate.
- **Final pose:** x≈5.81, y≈−1.10, z=1.50, heading≈+36°, holding at zero velocity (final decision was a hold, no gate/penguin in view).
- **Outcome:** task not completed. Only the left gate was plausibly crossed; the center gate was never located, and the flight exhausted its 14 decisions searching a dead-end alcove instead of finding it, so no penguin hover was attempted.

Biggest loss of decisions was early: 5 of the first 6 calls went into repeated yaw hunting on the left gate's posts (proximity made a near post swing wildly across the frame on small turns), which used almost a third of the budget before the first crossing.
